**4. Correct radius and K2 conjugacy; incorrect strict h3 face.** Def.5.1(1) gives g multiplicities72 at D2 and24 at D1. For h2 the corresponding multiplicities are24 and8. The latter can also be obtained from the source'"'s reduced common factor and canonical cube-root theorem, with complete coherent systems as below. With "'`A2=3`, a nonzero child residue alpha has conjugates `alpha,omega*alpha,omega''^2*alpha`. A zero residue cannot have multiplicity8 in a polynomial whose exponents are divisible by3. Three nonzero conjugates of multiplicity8 exhaust degree24. Consequently

```text
face_D2(K2) = (pi''^3-beta)''^8,  beta=alpha''^3 != 0.
