The engine has beta1 and kappa0. This contradicts source coverage on both branches, independently of jet0 and Hc. `forced_face_control.py` checks the comparison over Q with beta symbolic; its negative control gives `-8` at the old face and its positive control gives0 at kappa `-8/3`. The next coefficient gives `U10=20*beta''^2/3-3*ell`, so ell must not be prematurely pinned to `20/9`; it remains free at this argument'"'s level.

This also explains why computational consistency of the output-coordinate change did not expose the defect. Ordinary Euclidean division can represent the desired low-q K2 outputs as C2*h3+C3 with the old h3. At t"'^4 it can divide `-8*z''^21` by `z''^8(1+z)''^3`, with quotient and remainder of degree10. But that C2 quotient has weights12 through52, all below the source floor64. The existing output chart allows this cancellation; it does not establish that the canonical source h3 has the pinned face. The exact division and its failed weight bound are included in `forced-face-control.json`. This distinguishes a valid algebraic coordinate change from a valid source-to-chart restriction.

